      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
